WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.500
How do you know your anchor is dragging?

2
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:04.450
Three signs.

3
00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:08.300
Your bearings or your GPS position keep changing.

4
00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:11.400
The rode jerks or vibrates in your hand.

5
00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:15.725
Or your boat lies at a different angle than the boats around you.

6
00:00:15.975 --> 00:00:19.525
The cure is more scope, or pick up and anchor again.

7
00:00:19.775 --> 00:00:23.025
Now the rule that has killed people who ignored it.

8
00:00:23.275 --> 00:00:25.400
Always anchor from the bow.

9
00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:27.500
Never from the stern.

10
00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:29.000
Why?

11
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.450
Your transom is low and square.

12
00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:38.775
Anchored by the stern, the waves break straight over it, and a small boat can be swamped in minutes.

13
00:00:39.025 --> 00:00:45.550
If your anchor hooks under a rock or a ledge, a trip line tied to its crown lets you pull it out backward.

14
00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:50.450
And when the weather is changing, somebody stays up and keeps an anchor watch.
